{
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "What Pass actually is"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pass is Pherus's identity platform: the thing that answers \"who is this person, and what are they allowed to do\" for every other Pherus product. It isn't one app. It's two apps working together: Infra, the actual identity server, and Accounts, the interface people use to manage their own identity."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "blockquote",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "No per-user billing. No vendor lock-in. No third party ever sees a Pherus user's credentials."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Two apps, one identity"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Infra runs at infra.pherus.org. It's a real, spec-compliant OAuth 2.1 and OpenID Connect provider built on better-auth, with an admin dashboard behind it for managing users, roles, and every application connected to it."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Accounts runs at account.pherus.org. It's the end-user side: the place someone goes to manage their own profile, security, and sessions, without ever touching Infra's admin surface. Splitting the two apart means the people running Pherus and the people using Pherus never share one interface awkwardly trying to serve both."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "How it works"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Any new Pherus product plugs into Pass the same way a third-party app offers \"Sign in with Google\": it registers as an OAuth client of Infra, gets a client ID and a hashed client secret, and redirects people to Infra to sign in. Infra checks the request against the same redirect-URL safety rules the OAuth spec requires, authenticates the person, and hands the product back a token instead of a password."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "From there, the product never sees or stores a password at all. Two-factor codes, passkeys, and session management all live in one place: Pass. Signing out of a device from Accounts revokes that session everywhere it matters, not just in whichever product happened to trigger it."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Features for people using Pherus products"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "bulletList",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "paragraph",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "text",
                                    "text": "Sign in once, and stay signed in everywhere Pass is registered as the identity provider."
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "paragraph",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "text",
                                    "text": "Turn on two-factor authentication or register a passkey, both optional, both fully supported end to end."
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "paragraph",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "text",
                                    "text": "See every device and session currently signed in, and revoke any single one individually, not just a blunt sign-out-everywhere button."
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "paragraph",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "text",
                                    "text": "Manage your own profile and security settings from one place, account.pherus.org, regardless of which Pherus product you actually came from."
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Features for running Pherus"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "bulletList",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "paragraph",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "text",
                                    "text": "Approve, edit, rotate, or remove any connected OAuth application from one console."
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "paragraph",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "text",
                                    "text": "Fixed, simple access model: admin or user, nothing more to configure or misconfigure."
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "paragraph",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "text",
                                    "text": "A real audit trail: recent authentication and admin events, and daily breakdowns by outcome, instead of guessing what happened."
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "paragraph",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "text",
                                    "text": "Client secrets are stored hashed, never in plain text, and sensitive endpoints are rate-limited by default."
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Technology used, and why"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pass isn't built on a single framework so much as a deliberate stack, chosen layer by layer."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Runtime and hosting"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Both Infra and Accounts run as Cloudflare Workers, backed by D1 (SQL database), KV (fast key-value storage), and R2 (object storage for files and avatars). Choosing Cloudflare means Pass runs close to users everywhere, without Pherus operating its own data centers, while still being fully self-hosted rather than handed off to an identity SaaS vendor."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Framework"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Both apps are built on TanStack Start, a full-stack React 19 framework with server-side rendering, plus TanStack Router and TanStack Query for routing and data fetching. One consistent stack across the admin dashboard and the end-user app means the same patterns, the same conventions, and far less code to maintain twice."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Identity engine"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The actual authentication logic runs on better-auth, an open-source auth engine, not a proprietary black box. On top of it, Infra runs a real OAuth 2.1 and OpenID Connect provider, plus dedicated plugins for two-factor authentication and WebAuthn passkeys. This is the same open standard other products use to offer things like \"Sign in with Google\": nothing proprietary, nothing Pherus-specific that a new product has to learn."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Interface"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Both apps share one UI kit, built on Base UI (not Radix, not react-aria-components) with HugeIcons for icons, Tailwind CSS v4 for styling, and Motion for animation. TypeScript and Zod validate everything end to end, from form input to server function to database row."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Why this stack specifically"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Every choice here trades a bit of convenience for control. Cloudflare over a bigger cloud vendor means lower cost and edge performance, at the price of running fewer exotic managed services. better-auth over a hosted identity SaaS means Pherus owns its own user data outright, at the price of Pherus also owning the operations. That trade is the whole point of Pass."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Benefits, and how good it actually is"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The direct benefit is simple: every new Pherus product gets a real, secure, standards-compliant login system on day one, for free, without writing a single line of authentication code. Two-factor authentication, passkeys, session management, and an OAuth provider all come included, already working, already tested in production by the products already using them."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The less obvious benefit is consistency. Security posture, session behavior, and account management work identically across every Pherus product, because they're not each reimplementing it slightly differently. A security fix made once in Pass reaches every product at once."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pros and cons"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Self-hosting an identity provider is a real trade-off, not a strictly better option in every direction. Here's the honest version:"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "table",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "tableRow",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "tableHeader",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "Pros"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "tableHeader",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "Cons"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "tableRow",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "No per-user or per-monthly-active-user fees, ever"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "Pherus carries the operational burden instead of a vendor"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "tableRow",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "Full control over the whole identity stack"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "No vendor support line to call when something breaks"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "tableRow",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "Nobody outside Pherus ever sees a user's credentials"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "No mature marketplace of prebuilt integrations to lean on"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "tableRow",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "Real open standards (OAuth 2.1, OIDC), not a proprietary protocol"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "No enterprise SSO connectors (SAML and similar) built yet"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "tableRow",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "One identity and one account across every Pherus product"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "Every new capability has to be built in-house, not bought"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "tableRow",
                    "content": [
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "A real audit trail of authentication and admin activity"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "tableCell",
                            "content": [
                                {
                                    "type": "paragraph",
                                    "content": [
                                        {
                                            "type": "text",
                                            "text": "Scaling and reliability are Pherus's responsibility, not a vendor SLA"
                                        }
                                    ]
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
                "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "How this compares to hosted identity platforms"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Most products in this space work the same basic way: you outsource identity to someone else's servers, and pay per active user for the privilege. That's a completely reasonable trade for a lot of teams. Pass makes a different one."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "table",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "tableRow",
                    "content": [
